sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-goals-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In the evolved neural cellular automaton, transfer entropy between stripes first flows mainly from the red to the white stripe and then reverses, suggesting that the 'organizer' region (a group of cells that instructively patterns others) changes over time and embryonic regions take turns driving large-scale patterning.";
    dc:type "simulation-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Simulated embryonic regions take turns acting as the organizer";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Pio-Lopez L, Bischof J, LaPalme JV, Levin M, “The scaling of goals from cellular to anatomical homeostasis: an evolutionary simulation, experiment and analysis”, Interface focus (2023), doi:10.1098/rsfs.2022.0072; section “Computational results › Information-theoretic analysis of the dynamics of the anatomical homeostasis”. Scope: In silico 2D neural cellular automata evolved for the French flag problem"
}
